				<r3d:description language="eng">Greenland Environmental Observatory (GEOSummit) provides long term year round data on core atmospheric measurements, spatial phenomena,  ice sheets, and the Arctic Environment.  These data are available to researchers through the National Science Foundation&#039;s Science Coordination Office (SCO) which coordinates all research at GEOSummit. Currently there is not a central platform for multi-collaborator data distribution. For specific information related to research it is recommended to contact investigators directly.</r3d:description>
